{
  "_about": "Game terms stay in English in every translation. Every Codex entry title (read from codex.json on each run) is a game term: the term itself is never translated -- in the Codex, in the text describing other entries, and in the app -- only the words around it. 'keep': named terms always kept in any form, and checked everywhere (Airborne, Atlas, Fire, Threshold, Mana, Power ...). Other Codex titles are checked where they are written as the term (capitalised, or linked in the Codex). 'codex_everyday_words': Codex titles that are also ordinary English words (you, here, top, card, search, tap the screen ...): kept where they mean the game's term, translated where they are ordinary words. 'keep_when_game_term': game actions and words kept where they mean the game's action or thing. 'terms': fixed translations, as \"English\": \"translation\". 'notes': how to write the language.",
